{"nodes": [{"id": "worklog_migration_runbook", "label": "Migration Runbook", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "worklog.md", "source_location": "lines 5-43", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A single status table replaced prose scattered through checkpoints, which stopped being trustworthy at migration 014; migrations 002 through 019 are ordered, additive and re-run safe."}, {"id": "worklog_schema_sql_end_state", "label": "schema.sql as End-State, Not Update Path", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "worklog.md", "source_location": "lines 40-43", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "schema.sql describes a scratch project's end state and now includes the RPCs it was missing, since a project built from the old copy could be read but never written to; setup.sql was deleted as a drifted subset."}, {"id": "worklog_smoke_test_guards", "label": "Smoke-Test Database Guards", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "worklog.md", "source_location": "lines 34-38", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "npm run test:smoke asserts ten live guards: no host token in the plans projection, refused forged host-token and member_ages writes, and participant RPCs rejecting foreign spots, dead rounds, empty names and premature ratings."}, {"id": "worklog_security_hardening", "label": "Security Hardening Pass 2026-08-10", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "worklog.md", "source_location": "lines 45-76", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every P0/P1 finding from the prior review was still open; each fix has the same shape \u2014 move a secret or a rule somewhere the client cannot reach."}, {"id": "worklog_host_token_isolation", "label": "Host Token Isolation (plan_host_tokens)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "worklog.md", "source_location": "lines 51-57", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "plans.host_token_hash was readable by any share-link visitor and broadcast over realtime, so it moved to an insert-only plan_host_tokens table with no select policy; patching individual select(\"*\") calls was rejected because the next one would reintroduce the leak."}, {"id": "worklog_participant_rpc_integrity", "label": "Participant RPC Integrity Validation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "worklog.md", "source_location": "lines 58-61", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Migration 018 validated only a token-hash regex and never read plans; the hardening added spot-in-plan membership, plan status, stage/phase agreement, pool bounds, winner-only rating and non-empty names."}, {"id": "worklog_member_ages_dob_record", "label": "Write-Once member_ages DOB Record", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "worklog.md", "source_location": "lines 62-68", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "DOB in auth user_metadata was rewritable by any signed-in browser, making the 13/18/21 gates self-certified; it now lives in member_ages written only by the write-once set_birth_date RPC, and safeAgeFromMetadata was replaced by memberAge() so no caller can read age from metadata again."}, {"id": "worklog_legacy_write_path_removal", "label": "Legacy Direct-Write Path Removal", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "worklog.md", "source_location": "lines 69-73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three direct-write fallbacks in the shared plan page were revoked by migration 015 and failing silently (the decide fallback never checked its error); they and the duplicate client tally were deleted so execute_plan_command is the sole tally, and the deadline auto-pick became host-only."}, {"id": "worklog_plan_creation_rollback", "label": "Plan Creation Rollback", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "worklog.md", "source_location": "lines 74-75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A failed plan_spots insert used to leave an unusable plan behind a live share link, so the plan row is now rolled back on failure."}, {"id": "worklog_rate_limiter_gap", "label": "In-Process Rate Limiter Gap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "worklog.md", "source_location": "lines 74-76, 197", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deliberately still open: rate limiters are in-process Maps that reset on cold start and the OTP limiter grows unbounded on attacker-supplied emails; distributed limiting is future work."}, {"id": "worklog_auth_deferral_scope", "label": "Deferred Authentication Scope", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "worklog.md", "source_location": "lines 102-107, 223-227", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Google OAuth is not enabled in the connected Supabase project (external.google: false), so product work should not block on external auth credentials; prioritize core planning, local/demo usage, recommendation quality, testing and security review instead."}, {"id": "worklog_next_agent_start_order", "label": "Next-Agent Start Order", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "worklog.md", "source_location": "lines 200-208", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Read the handoff and CHECKPOINT.md instead of rescanning the repo, fix host-token exposure first, harden participant RPCs with negative tests, design the protected DOB record, then run the full verification set and update both logs."}], "edges": [{"source": "worklog_auth_deferral_scope", "target": "auth_setup_google_oauth", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "s